1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:02,920
What if Earth stopped spinning?

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,840
Right now, you're moving.

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:12,280
At the equator, Earth's surface spins at about 1,670 km/h. You just can't feel it.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:14,600
Now imagine it slowing down.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,520
The days get longer.

6
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:21,800
It's already happening. Every century, the day gets about 2 milliseconds longer.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,970
1.4 billion years ago, a day lasted only about 18 hours.

8
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:29,640
Then it stops.

9
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:32,440
Now one day lasts a whole year.

10
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:38,520
The Sun would rise and set just once a year. 6 months of daylight. 6 months of night.

11
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,880
The Sun hangs in the sky. It doesn't move.

12
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,640
The ground bakes.

13
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:47,480
Without the spin, Earth's oceans would drain toward the poles.

14
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:50,840
Then, finally, the Sun starts to set.

15
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,600
And the night begins.

16
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,240
With no sunlight for months, the night side would plunge far below freezing.

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:02,268
For anything that hunts in the dark, this is the longest night there has ever been.

18
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:06,382
And something has been waiting for it.

19
00:01:08,221 --> 00:01:10,241
Wait.

20
00:01:10,741 --> 00:01:13,841
What if the Moon crashed into Earth?

21
00:01:14,441 --> 00:01:17,750
What if Earth stopped spinning?
